(a) The Equal Opportunity Council shall:
(1) Make careful and comprehensive surveys and studies of existing local problems of poverty;
(2) Propose local action programs designed to improve economic opportunity for low-income families;
(3) Prepare priority listings for such local action programs;
(4) Prepare community action programs applications for federal assistance under the Economic Opportunity Act of 1964; and
(5) Assist in carrying out such local community action programs approved by the government of the United States of America.
(b) Community action program applications shall be subject to the final approval of the Macon-Bibb County Commission prior to transmission to the state and federal office of economic opportunity. In general, the council shall have such powers as may be needed to recommend the necessary local action programs and to carry out the programs as shall from time to time be determined jointly by the governing authority of Macon-Bibb County; provided, however, it will not be necessary for grantees to obtain the approval of the governing authorities of Macon-Bibb County for those programs which will not require a contribution from such local authority to the nonfederal share necessary to qualify for a federal grant for such program.
